WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.557
There is a perspective now suggesting

00:00:02.557 --> 00:00:05.144
that in the 1980s, industrial upgrading

00:00:05.144 --> 00:00:07.666
was like a focused beam that benefited

00:00:07.666 --> 00:00:10.188
80%of the population, whereas the 2026

00:00:10.188 --> 00:00:12.580
AI boom is like a massive cloud, yet

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.167
only 10%of people in the ICT sector are

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.051
benefiting.

00:00:16.051 --> 00:00:18.257
>> We also know that AI policies are

00:00:18.257 --> 00:00:20.659
rapidly absorbing massive amounts of

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:23.191
water, electricity, and human resources

00:00:23.191 --> 00:00:25.527
, and are even driving up financial

00:00:25.527 --> 00:00:27.570
lending. As a result, with so many

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.759
resources tilting toward AI, many polls

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:31.730
in the U.S. have already shown that

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.755
those who oppose AI data centers now

00:00:33.755 --> 00:00:35.990
outnumber those who support them. Given

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.794
that your policy direction is to

00:00:37.794 --> 00:00:39.982
promote AI, how do you plan to strike a

00:00:39.982 --> 00:00:40.520
balance?

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.946
>> Thank you for this question. I am fully

00:00:42.946 --> 00:00:45.193
aware that the world has entered the

00:00:45.193 --> 00:00:47.618
era of artificial intelligence. That is

00:00:47.618 --> 00:00:49.610
why, at the beginning of my term, I

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.895
actively pushed for legislation. It is

00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:54.380
called the Basic Law for Artificial

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.142
Intelligence, which rests on seven core

00:00:57.142 --> 00:01:00.620
principles. These principles state that

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.284
as we promote AI development, the first

00:01:03.284 --> 00:01:05.881
priority is social sustainability, and

00:01:05.881 --> 00:01:08.478
the second is human autonomy, ensuring

00:01:08.478 --> 00:01:11.690
we don't end up being controlled by AI.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:12.760
>> Mm.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.471
>> The third principle is privacy, as data

00:01:15.471 --> 00:01:18.047
is the most crucial element of AI, so

00:01:18.047 --> 00:01:20.690
we must be mindful of data acquisition

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.689
and ownership. The fourth is security;

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:27.799
security is extremely important.

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:29.901
>> The fifth is transparency and

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:32.565
explainability, and the sixth is that

00:01:32.565 --> 00:01:34.948
we must ensure fairness and avoid

00:01:34.948 --> 00:01:37.952
discrimination.

00:01:37.952 --> 00:01:40.190
>> That covers the sixth and seventh,

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:42.683
which is accountability. So, as you can

00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:44.858
see, My answer is that the government

00:01:44.858 --> 00:01:47.160
must act as a responsible promoter. The

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.006
seven principles mentioned above are

00:01:49.006 --> 00:01:51.559
our way of being responsible. Mm.

00:01:51.559 --> 00:01:53.678
>> Secondly, the government must, of

00:01:53.678 --> 00:01:56.109
course, promote the development of AI,

00:01:56.109 --> 00:01:58.478
but we will do so steadily within the

00:01:58.478 --> 00:02:01.021
framework of these seven principles. As

00:02:01.021 --> 00:02:03.471
you just mentioned, we have proposed

00:02:03.471 --> 00:02:05.988
the "AI New Ten Major Constructions,"

00:02:05.988 --> 00:02:08.239
which include four infrastructure

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:10.822
foundations: the first is human talent

00:02:10.822 --> 00:02:13.338
cultivation, aiming to train at least

00:02:13.338 --> 00:02:16.088
500,000 AI application talents by 2040.

00:02:16.088 --> 00:02:18.432
The second is to build centers for

00:02:18.432 --> 00:02:21.112
computing power and AI sovereignty; the

00:02:21.112 --> 00:02:23.792
third is stable electricity supply; and

00:02:23.792 --> 00:02:26.003
the fourth is to ensure balanced

00:02:26.003 --> 00:02:28.512
development across Taiwan. Of course,

00:02:28.512 --> 00:02:30.938
the AI New Ten Major Constructions also

00:02:30.938 --> 00:02:33.244
focus on three key core technologies:

00:02:33.244 --> 00:02:35.549
silicon photonics, quantum computing,

00:02:35.549 --> 00:02:38.077
and robotics. Ultimately, we hope to

00:02:38.077 --> 00:02:40.636
achieve three goals. The first is to

00:02:40.636 --> 00:02:43.090
assist at least one million small and

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.415
medium-sized enterprises by 2040 in

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:47.740
adopting artificial intelligence so

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.936
they can successfully upgrade and

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:53.936
transform.
